From 35d69a793660ae58ce115776678e4d778dbfc045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:36:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] drm/asahi: g17: M5: Build the 27.2 (26B123) InitData
 graph

The M5 GPU firmware of macOS 27.2 (26B123, RTKit pac-3514.41.1) checks
root+0 against 0x0c8e_4339_8728_04c0, where 27.0 (26A428) checks
0x0c8e_0339_8728_04c0: only bit 46 differs. Its kext writes that word
with the movk sequence at AGXG17X 0xfffffe0008bb8bac..0xfffffe0008bb8bbc
(26A428: 0xfffffe0008ba77cc..0xfffffe0008ba77dc).

Its allocation size table, the u64[24] at AGXG17X __TEXT,__const
0xfffffe0007153188 in both kexts, differs from 26A428's
(ABI_ALLOCATION_SIZES_26A428_M5, read at the same address) in two
entries only:

  index 4,  power policy:  0x126b0 -> 0x12728
  index 13, status config: 0x780   -> 0x790

The packed layouts derived from it move accordingly: in the shared
cluster everything after the policy moves by 0x80 (views 3 and 4, the
BRN table and repeated region, the twelve DM rings, both main configs
and control rings); in the private cluster everything after the status
config moves by 0x40 (both role sets with status A, the secondary
control state, secondary extra 1 and the policy state). Both clusters
keep their page-rounded sizes (0x34000 and 0x178000), so the fixed
windows of the M5 graph still hold them. The HW data of 26B123 is
26A428's: the store tracker finds the same 340 HW data stores at the
same offsets in both kexts.

Describe one firmware build's InitData layout as an M5Layout (its size
table, the packed clusters derived from it, and how its HW data moves
relative to the 26A428 encoding), add M5_LAYOUT_26A428 and
M5_LAYOUT_26B123, and a RootProfile J714G17S26B123 that writes the new
version word and takes its offsets from the 26B123 layout. build_m5()
now takes the firmware build's Variant and builds the profile its
M5Layouts names, so the 26B123 build admitted by the firmware identity
runs this graph, and Gpu::new() refuses only a build that names no M5
layouts. The 26A428 encodings are unchanged: a standalone check, run on
this series, compiles the whole g17/fw/m5/initdata.rs before and after
with rustc and compares the HW data of every board, the private
cluster, the bundle policy, both roots and both main configs byte for
byte.

Not part of this change, and needed before 26B123 can run: the moved
power policy words (from 0x4910 on) and the re-laid-out status config
(0x5c4 on, including the link word and pointer), whose layouts are
measured separately.

